<<
/Title (Classification is a data mining technique used to predict group membership for data instances. It is a form of supervised learning where a model is trained on a labeled dataset \(i.e., data with known class labels\), and then used to classify new, unseen instances into predefined categories or classes. For example, a classification algorithm could be used to predict whether an email is spam or not based on its content.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1175 0 R
>>
